  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar Earthquake Acute Crisis Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IRC will implement an integrated multi-sectoral emergency response in the affected urban and rural areas of Mandalay and Sagaing regions. IRC provides health, protection and MPCA and will coordinate with other JR members and actors. Health: IRC deploys 2 Mobile Medical Teams (MMT), incl. 1 medical doctor, 2 nurses, 1 health counsellor and 1 health promotor, providing emergency primary healthcare and MHPSS services and referrals based on IRC/health sector guidelines. IRC procures medical supplies as well as uses pre-existing stock to ensure that the MMTs are equipped, reaching 10,000 (4,680 male and 5,320 female). MPCA: Markets are sufficiently functioning esp. in Mandalay town, which makes it possible to provide MPCA to 1347 HHs, 5,666 individuals, to enable them to meet their immediate needs. Protection: IRC will conduct emergency protection monitoring (PM) and protection mainstreaming activities based on Global Protection Cluster Mainstreaming toolkit, reaching 2,000 people. The protection team while conducting the PM will coordinate with health and cash team as well as other JR members for the referrals of the individuals identified with specific needs for healthcare or basic needs.</narrative>
  </description>
